rules.rule:
PRE-PASS (affects list indentation). Before block parsing: (1) CRLF/CR -> LF; (2) "

" appended to the source; (3) the WHOLE source (newlines included) is tab-expanded with tab stop 4 — i.e. per line, each TAB advances the column to the next multiple of 4; (4) `re.sub(r'(?<=
) +
', '
')` — any line that consists solely of one-or-more spaces is replaced by an empty line (this does NOT apply to the very first line of the document, which has no preceding 
). Consequence: a TAB right after a list marker at column 0 becomes 3 spaces (`*` at col 0, tab -> col 4), one leading TAB becomes 4 spaces (a valid nesting indent), two leading TABs become 8 spaces. A spaces-only separator line counts as a truly blank line.
